# Frequency comparison within one unit

Verifies equality and ordering between hertz values without unit scaling. Distinct operands exercise `==`, `!=`, `<`, and `>`, while reflexive operands pin the inclusive ordering boundaries.

>>> source
small: int = 500hz
large: int = 1000hz
print(small == large)
print(small != large)
print(small < large)
print(large > small)
print(small <= small)
print(large >= large)

<<< stdout
false
true
true
true
true
true

<<< stderr
